1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,700
Meet Lodestone. A native Minecraft launcher, built in Rust.

2
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:10,000
Every instance lives in one library: Fabric, Forge, NeoForge, Quilt, or vanilla.

3
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:14,800
Each one gets its own artwork, its playtime, and a one-click Play button.

4
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:19,900
Discover searches Modrinth, CurseForge, ATLauncher, Technic, and FTB.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,300
Five platforms, without ever leaving the launcher.

6
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:27,600
Looking for something specific? Results land as you type,

7
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:31,200
filtered to your game version and loader.

8
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:36,000
Every project gets a full page: its description, screenshots,

9
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,700
changelogs, and every version, so you know what you're installing.

10
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:44,600
Starting fresh takes seconds. Name it, pick a Minecraft version,

11
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:48,700
choose a loader, and Lodestone matches the right Java for you.

12
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:54,200
Inside an instance, everything is within reach. Switch mods on and off,

13
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:59,200
browse its files, check its worlds, and tune its settings.

14
00:01:00,100 --> 00:01:04,400
The Worlds page gathers every save from every instance.

15
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:09,000
Filter by game mode, search by name or seed, or switch to a table.

16
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:13,900
Servers show live pings, player counts, and their message of the day,

17
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:17,700
refreshed on their own, with LAN games right alongside.

18
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:23,500
And your skin gets a 3D preview you can spin and try on.

19
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:30,100
Plus imports from other launchers, modpack exports, portable builds, and mod snapshots you can roll back.

20
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:35,800
Lodestone. Free and open source, at lodestonelauncher.com.
